---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ArchitectureDiagram from "../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import ExternalLink from "../components/ExternalLink.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
import { urls, sourceUrl } from "../site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Messaging across a shared fabric"
  description="EpochGrid combines NATS infrastructure with MLS end-to-end group encryption. Explore the architecture, implemented capabilities, and developer workflow."
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open source / distributed messaging</p>
      <h1>
        Shared infrastructure.
        <br />
        <span>Endpoint encryption.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        EpochGrid combines NATS messaging infrastructure with MLS end-to-end
        group encryption. The fabric routes and stores messages. Devices hold
        the keys and read the content.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/architecture/">
          Explore the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="button" href="/developers/">
          Developer guide
        </a>
        <ExternalLink href={urls.source}>View on GitHub</ExternalLink>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-note">
      <span class="technical">Project snapshot / 01</span>
      <div class="topology" aria-hidden="true">
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
        <i></i>
      </div>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Transport</dt>
          <dd>NATS + JetStream</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Encryption</dt>
          <dd>MLS via OpenMLS</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Implementation</dt>
          <dd>Rust · CLI + TUI</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Callout title="MVP implemented · alpha preparation in progress">
      <p>
        The tested MVP now includes receipts, replies, edits, reactions and
        explicitly invited service participants. Dynamic admission works;
        dynamic CLI/TUI messaging is not yet supported. Typing UI is deferred.
        No alpha release is tagged, and the system remains unaudited.{" "}
        <a href="/project/#current-status">
          Read the current scope and limitations →
        </a>
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </div>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Purpose</p>
      <h2>Why EpochGrid?</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Separate the messaging fabric from the keys that make a conversation
        readable.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="three-columns">
      <div>
        <span class="index">01</span>
        <h3>Infrastructure has a defined role</h3>
        <p>
          NATS handles routing and persistence. The metadata backend manages
          public identity and authorization state without decrypting chat. An
          invited service participant is a separate, readable endpoint.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="index">02</span>
        <h3>Group state stays at the edge</h3>
        <p>
          OpenMLS manages cryptographic membership. Independent device keys and
          authenticated Welcome messages connect directory identity to the
          group.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="index">03</span>
        <h3>Failure is part of the workflow</h3>
        <p>
          Durable inboxes, a ciphertext outbox and local transactions support
          offline catch-up and tested process restart boundaries.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Implementation</p>
      <h2>A working, deliberately scoped system</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      {[
        [
          "Identity and discovery",
          "Independent keys, signed registration and enrollment, plus device revocation with broker exclusion and coordinated MLS removal.",
        ],
        [
          "Encrypted group messages",
          "Authenticated Welcome joining and MLS PrivateMessages, with coordinator-serialized membership changes.",
        ],
        [
          "Durable delivery and history",
          "JetStream ciphertext, retryable sends, local transcripts and offline catch-up.",
        ],
        [
          "A persistent terminal client",
          "Channel navigation, message composition, history, unread counts and automatic reconnect.",
        ],
        [
          "Independent devices",
          "Separate keys and state per device, explicit invitations and ordered membership catch-up.",
        ],
        [
          "Device verification",
          "Manual fingerprint comparison, persistent key-change warnings and a signed registration log with locally retained checkpoints.",
        ],
        [
          "Encrypted identity recovery",
          "Client-encrypted control credentials and trust evidence. Resuming messaging requires a fresh device and invitation; old chat keys and history are excluded.",
        ],
        [
          "Delivery and read receipts",
          "Encrypted device claims distinguish server acceptance, delivery and local presentation. Read is not proof of human attention.",
        ],
        [
          "Replies, edits and reactions",
          "Stable application IDs and authenticated, append-only relationships. Edits preserve original history.",
        ],
        [
          "Explicit service participants",
          "An invited MLS endpoint can answer status requests. It reads its joined conversation; the metadata backend does not.",
        ],
        [
          "Dynamic admission",
          "Canonical user/device enrollment and expiring Auth Callout grants. Full dynamic messaging integration remains in progress.",
        ],
        [
          "Encrypted attachments",
          "Client-encrypted files in NATS Object Store; metadata and keys inside MLS. Explicit authenticated saves, with size and retention limits.",
        ],
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <div>
          <StatusBadge status="implemented" />
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p>{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="fine">
      Implemented describes repository code, not production readiness. The full
      messaging flow currently runs in the explicit static development fixture.{" "}
      <ExternalLink href={sourceUrl("docs/mvp-acceptance.md")}>
        Acceptance evidence
      </ExternalLink>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <ExternalLink href={sourceUrl("docs/tui.md")}>
        Terminal client
      </ExternalLink>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <ExternalLink href={sourceUrl("docs/device-verification.md")}>
        Verification and log limits
      </ExternalLink>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <ExternalLink href={sourceUrl("README.md")}>
        Milestone status
      </ExternalLink>
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Callout title="Toward the MVP/production alpha">
      <p>
        <StatusBadge status="experimental" /> Milestone 22 has signed group
        policies, exact subject grants and transactional revocation. Client
        policy synchronization, filtered consumers and Welcome relay remain
        unfinished. Protected local storage, deployment validation and release
        artifacts are still alpha gates.{" "}
        <a href="/project/#toward-the-mvpproduction-alpha">
          Read the release direction and remaining gaps →
        </a>
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </div>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Message path</p>
      <h2>One fabric. Distinct trust boundaries.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Content encryption, broker permissions and local storage provide
        different protections.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ArchitectureDiagram />
    <a class="text-link" href="/architecture/">
      Inspect the security layers →
    </a>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Foundations</p>
      <h2>A small set of substantial building blocks</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="stack-strip">
      <div>
        <strong>Rust</strong>
        <span>Shared core, CLI and service</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>NATS</strong>
        <span>Transport and durable streams</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>OpenMLS</strong>
        <span>Group cryptographic state</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>SQLite</strong>
        <span>Transactional device storage</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link" href="/technology/">
      Roles, rationale and tradeoffs →
    </a>
  </section>
  <section class="contribute wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Build with the project</p>
    <h2>Start with the code. Help refine the boundaries.</h2>
    <p>
      Run the development flow, examine the threat model, or discuss a focused
      change with the maintainers.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/developers/">
        Get started →
      </a>
      <ExternalLink href={urls.contributing}>
        Contribution guidelines
      </ExternalLink>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
